  "result": "I fixed all three problems in `src/queue.js`, and `npm test` passes (6 of 6).\n\n- **Hang after a failure:** a rejected job never freed its slot, so `running` stayed too high and the queue stalled. A job that throws synchronously, or returns a plain value, also broke it. Now every job is wrapped, so success and failure both free the slot and start the next job. A failing job still rejects only its own promise.\n- **`onIdle()` resolving too early:** it only checked that nothing was pending. It now also requires `running === 0`.\n- **One job at a time after `pause()`/`resume()`:** `next()` started at most one job per call. It now loops until all free slots are filled, up to `concurrency`.\n\nI added four regression tests in `test/queue.test.js`:\n- The queue keeps going after a job rejects, throws synchronously, or returns a plain value.\n- `onIdle()` waits for running jobs, and resolves immediately when already idle.\n- `onIdle()` resolves after a failing job.\n- After `resume()` with concurrency 4, four jobs run at once and never more than four.",
